---
functor: 1
title: paren
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`paren` · fence · round brackets, a group or a tuple.

# Form

`(a + b).paren` on a group, `x.paren` on a symbol.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `(a + b).paren` | $(a + b).paren$ | fence around the group |
| `(frac(1, 2)).paren` | $(frac(1, 2)).paren$ | fence around the group |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Round brackets, a group or a tuple. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | A kind can take this fence from a rule: `set abs(fence: paren)`. |
| Construction | Brackets around a group or a symbol. The brackets grow with the content. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- Works on a group, `(a + b).paren`, or on a symbol, `x.paren`. Write `x2` after it to double the fence. Write `left` or `right` after it to keep one side only. A style rule can give a kind its fence: `set mat(fence: paren)`.

# From LaTeX

`\left( x \right)` becomes `(x).paren`, or just `(x)`.

